 "central_question": "Off Suffolk in June 2024 a Border Force cutter closed on an inflatable carrying about 350 kg of cocaine under a tarp. His crewmate jumped and swam; Bruce Knowles restarted the engines and ran, grounded the boat on a beach and jumped into the sea. He pleaded guilty and got 17 years and 3 months; the swimmer, caught that day, got 15. Throttle or swim for it?",
