 "content_notes": "Tone: dry and quick; the joke is on the scheme (an inflatable trying to outrun a cutter and ending on a beach), never on a person; no one was hurt (none reported), and the jumps are drawn as acts, not falls. Bruce Knowles pleaded guilty and was sentenced (Ipswich Crown Court, Aug 2024 and May 2025) and is named by the NCA and the press, so he is named, but only on a label (never in the narration); he is drawn ONLY as a dark rim-lit silhouette (NOT A LIKENESS). His crewmate is never named and is drawn only as a silhouette. Border Force officers, the police officer and the judge are generic figures with no badge, patch, crest, flag, agency name or insignia; no weapon; no force shown. The RHIB and the cutter are generic (no name, number, livery or flag); the tarp's colour is not reported (drawn orange); the bales are plain dark wrapped blocks; no drugs are shown. The time of day is not reported: the quay is drawn under a floodlight and the chase in a grey low light; no line or caption states a time. Nothing copies the NCA footage. Every card is our own typed graphic; no court document is imitated; no dialogue is invented. Facts verified 2026-10-30.",
